A comforting baked pasta featuring penne enrobed in slow-simmered sausage marinara, layered with creamy ricotta and gooey melted mozzarella.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a29777181/classic-mostaccioli-recipe/).*

## Ingredients

- 2 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil
- 1 lb. sweet Italian sausage, removed from casings
- 2 cloves garlic, minced
- ⅛ teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes
- 1 can (28 oz) whole peeled tomatoes, pulsed in a blender until smooth
- 1 sprig fresh basil, plus extra chopped for garnish
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- 8 oz. penne or mostaccioli pasta
- 1 large egg
- 1 cup whole-milk ricotta cheese
- ½ cup freshly grated Parmesan cheese, divided
- 1 ½ cups shredded mozzarella cheese, divided

## Instructions

1. **Simmer the Meat Sauce:** In a medium saucepan over medium heat, warm the olive oil. Add the sweet Italian sausage, breaking it up with a wooden spoon, and cook until browned, about 8 minutes. Stir in the minced garlic and crushed red pepper flakes; cook until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Pour in the pureed tomatoes and submerge the fresh basil sprig. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to medium-low and simmer uncovered for 15 minutes until slightly thickened. Season with salt and black pepper to taste, then discard the basil sprig.
2. **Boil the Pasta:** Preheat your oven to 450°F (230°C). Bring a large pot of salted water to a rolling boil. Cook the pasta until just al dente (about 2 minutes shy of package instructions) so it holds its shape during baking. Drain well.
3. **Mix the Ricotta:** In a small mixing bowl, beat the egg lightly. Stir in the ricotta, ¼ cup of the grated Parmesan, and ½ cup of the mozzarella. Season lightly with salt and pepper.
4. **Layer the Casserole:** Spread a thin ladle of meat sauce across the bottom of a 2-quart baking dish. Arrange the drained pasta over the sauce. Dollop the ricotta mixture evenly across the pasta, then spoon the remaining meat sauce over top. Finish by sprinkling with the remaining ¼ cup Parmesan and remaining 1 cup mozzarella.
5. **Bake:** Bake uncovered at 450°F for about 15 minutes until the cheese is bubbling and top is deeply golden brown. Garnish with chopped fresh basil and let stand 5 minutes before serving.

## Notes

- **Pasta Shapes:** Mostaccioli (smooth tubular pasta) and penne rigate (ridged penne) are interchangeable here.
- **High Heat Finish:** Baking at 450°F gives a quick, bubbly melt and blistered golden cheese crust without drying out the noodles.
